{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31c4-7192-b2b8-2cf96a27b509","id":"01a1a635-32f0-76a2-8827-3c038be4faee","idempotency_key":"f523bf09e54dffa77a3e821cbebe1096dbbaccd395929089416217b0d9af1921","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T10:57:46Z","payload":{"note":"Three of five. GET /api/ai/ratings is the ladder: rating, deviation, conservative rank (rating - 2*RD), games and the last change from the ledger. GET /api/ai/metrics aggregates per model from two sources - turns (tokens in/out, errors, average latency, duration) and the stored matches (plies and legal rate). Legal rate needed a real change: every model ply now records how many replies it took (MatchMove.attempts, set by the play driver through Match::note_attempts), because a legal rate cannot be inferred after the fact from a move list that only kept the final answer. The Play tab renders a leaderboard with a competitor filter and a legal-rate column, and a tournaments panel (create a round robin, list, step/pause/resume, standings table). Browser check: frontend/tests/cdp/cdp_leaderboard.js -> AI_LEADERBOARD_PASS. That check caught a real bug: tournament_action reused match_action, so Step and Pause posted to /api/ai/matches/{id}/{action}, the buttons appeared to work and nothing happened - the message never changed. It has its own path now. STILL OPEN: i-c857 (per-turn caps exist as TurnLimits and a tournament has a hard budget that pauses at the cap, but there is no per-session cap) and i-c8a8 (the leaderboard shows the legal rate but not tokens/cost; per-turn usage is already in the Assistant transcript).","target":"t-a488"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
